IMPORT policy

-- Nine blind benchmark queries (Kant et al. 2025, Appendix A.2), each encoded
-- as a Claim and run through policy's `covered`. Standing preamble applied to
-- every query: "Assuming all other conditions are met and no other exclusions
-- apply (where by 'other' I mean anything not referenced in the query that
-- follows)." The agreement-signed and premium-paid assumptions are already
-- built into policy.l4 unconditionally, so they need no field here.
--
-- Baseline values used whenever a query does not speak to that fact (chosen so
-- every condition unrelated to the query holds, and no unrelated exclusion
-- fires):
--   age at hospitalization ........................... 30   (well under the age-80 exclusion)
--   months after effective date of hospitalization ... 3    (within both the 7- and 12-month windows)
--   hospital located in the United States ............ TRUE
--   wellness visit confirmation supplied ............. JUST 1 (month after the effective date)
--   all four "caused by ..." exclusion flags ......... FALSE
--   fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding FALSE
--   claim made to the company with basis stated ...... TRUE

-- Q1. Will my policy apply if I was hospitalized by burns suffered while doing
--     my duty as a firefighter?
-- The burns arose directly out of firefighter service, so Section 3.1(3)
-- excludes the claim outright.
q1 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                                                       IS 30
    `months after the effective date the hospitalization occurred`                 IS 3
    `due to sickness`                                                              IS FALSE
    `due to accidental injury`                                                     IS TRUE
    `hospital located in the United States`                                        IS TRUE
    `caused by skydiving`                                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the military`                                            IS FALSE
    `caused by service as a fire fighter`                                          IS TRUE
    `caused by service in the police`                                              IS FALSE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding`                           IS FALSE
    `months after the effective date the wellness visit confirmation was supplied` IS JUST 1
    `claim made to the company with the basis for the claim stated`                IS TRUE
#EVAL `covered` q1

-- Q2. Will my policy apply if I am 78 years old at the time of hospitalization?
-- 78 is below the Section 3.1(5) age-80 threshold. No cause of hospitalization
-- is referenced by the query, so a generic covered event is assumed.
q2 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                                                       IS 78
    `months after the effective date the hospitalization occurred`                 IS 3
    `due to sickness`                                                              IS TRUE
    `due to accidental injury`                                                     IS FALSE
    `hospital located in the United States`                                        IS TRUE
    `caused by skydiving`                                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the military`                                            IS FALSE
    `caused by service as a fire fighter`                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the police`                                              IS FALSE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding`                           IS FALSE
    `months after the effective date the wellness visit confirmation was supplied` IS JUST 1
    `claim made to the company with the basis for the claim stated`                IS TRUE
#EVAL `covered` q2

-- Q3. Will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for pneumonia 5 months after
--     the policy's effective date, and my age at the time of hospitalization
--     is 65?
-- Pneumonia is a sickness. 5 months is within both the 7-month Section 1.3
-- window and the 12-month policy term. Age 65 is below the exclusion
-- threshold.
q3 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                                                       IS 65
    `months after the effective date the hospitalization occurred`                 IS 5
    `due to sickness`                                                              IS TRUE
    `due to accidental injury`                                                     IS FALSE
    `hospital located in the United States`                                        IS TRUE
    `caused by skydiving`                                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the military`                                            IS FALSE
    `caused by service as a fire fighter`                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the police`                                              IS FALSE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding`                           IS FALSE
    `months after the effective date the wellness visit confirmation was supplied` IS JUST 1
    `claim made to the company with the basis for the claim stated`                IS TRUE
#EVAL `covered` q3

-- Q4. Will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to a fall while
--     traveling abroad and I had given confirmation of my wellness visit 8
--     months after the policy's effective date?
-- Two independent problems. First, confirmation at 8 months misses the
-- Section 1.3 seven-month deadline, so Section 1.2's second cancelation
-- ground is triggered. Second, being hospitalized "while traveling abroad" is
-- read here as the confinement itself taking place outside the United
-- States, so Section 2.2's "hospital in the United States" condition on the
-- daily benefit also fails -- Section 4.1.1's worldwide insuring language
-- does not override that narrower condition (see the note in policy.l4).
q4 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                                                       IS 30
    `months after the effective date the hospitalization occurred`                 IS 3
    `due to sickness`                                                              IS FALSE
    `due to accidental injury`                                                     IS TRUE
    `hospital located in the United States`                                        IS FALSE
    `caused by skydiving`                                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the military`                                            IS FALSE
    `caused by service as a fire fighter`                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the police`                                              IS FALSE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding`                           IS FALSE
    `months after the effective date the wellness visit confirmation was supplied` IS JUST 8
    `claim made to the company with the basis for the claim stated`                IS TRUE
#EVAL `covered` q4

-- Q5. Will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for punching my own face to
--     show off for my friends and I did not commit fraud or misrepresentation?
-- Judgement call (see NOTES.md): a deliberate act performed on oneself to
-- show off is neither a "sickness" nor an "accidental injury" under Section
-- 2.1 -- the injury was the knowing result of a voluntary act, not an
-- accident. So the Section 2.1 trigger for any benefit is never reached. The
-- "no fraud" fact only heads off Section 1.2's first cancelation ground; it
-- does not supply a triggering event.
q5 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                                                       IS 30
    `months after the effective date the hospitalization occurred`                 IS 3
    `due to sickness`                                                              IS FALSE
    `due to accidental injury`                                                     IS FALSE
    `hospital located in the United States`                                        IS TRUE
    `caused by skydiving`                                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the military`                                            IS FALSE
    `caused by service as a fire fighter`                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the police`                                              IS FALSE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding`                           IS FALSE
    `months after the effective date the wellness visit confirmation was supplied` IS JUST 1
    `claim made to the company with the basis for the claim stated`                IS TRUE
#EVAL `covered` q5

-- Q6. Will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to an injury sustained
--     while skydiving, my age at the time of hospitalization was 79, and
--     proof of my wellness visit was provided 6.5 months after the policy's
--     effective date?
-- Skydiving is excluded outright by Section 3.1(1), regardless of the other,
-- individually-satisfied facts (age 79 is under 80; 6.5 months is within the
-- Section 1.3 window).
q6 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                                                       IS 79
    `months after the effective date the hospitalization occurred`                 IS 3
    `due to sickness`                                                              IS FALSE
    `due to accidental injury`                                                     IS TRUE
    `hospital located in the United States`                                        IS TRUE
    `caused by skydiving`                                                          IS TRUE
    `caused by service in the military`                                            IS FALSE
    `caused by service as a fire fighter`                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the police`                                              IS FALSE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding`                           IS FALSE
    `months after the effective date the wellness visit confirmation was supplied` IS JUST 6.5
    `claim made to the company with the basis for the claim stated`                IS TRUE
#EVAL `covered` q6

-- Q7. Will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for a heart attack, proof of
--     the wellness visit was submitted 2 months after the policy's effective
--     date, and my age at the time of hospitalization was 75?
-- A heart attack is a sickness. 2 months is comfortably within the Section
-- 1.3 window. Age 75 is below the exclusion threshold.
q7 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                                                       IS 75
    `months after the effective date the hospitalization occurred`                 IS 3
    `due to sickness`                                                              IS TRUE
    `due to accidental injury`                                                     IS FALSE
    `hospital located in the United States`                                        IS TRUE
    `caused by skydiving`                                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the military`                                            IS FALSE
    `caused by service as a fire fighter`                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the police`                                              IS FALSE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding`                           IS FALSE
    `months after the effective date the wellness visit confirmation was supplied` IS JUST 2
    `claim made to the company with the basis for the claim stated`                IS TRUE
#EVAL `covered` q7

-- Q8. Will my policy apply if I was hospitalized after being injured in a
--     military training exercise, the hospitalization occurred within the
--     policy term, and I did not commit fraud?
-- The injury arose directly out of military service, so Section 3.1(2)
-- excludes the claim outright, regardless of the term and no-fraud facts.
q8 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                                                       IS 30
    `months after the effective date the hospitalization occurred`                 IS 3
    `due to sickness`                                                              IS FALSE
    `due to accidental injury`                                                     IS TRUE
    `hospital located in the United States`                                        IS TRUE
    `caused by skydiving`                                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the military`                                            IS TRUE
    `caused by service as a fire fighter`                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the police`                                              IS FALSE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding`                           IS FALSE
    `months after the effective date the wellness visit confirmation was supplied` IS JUST 1
    `claim made to the company with the basis for the claim stated`                IS TRUE
#EVAL `covered` q8

-- Q9. Will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to my son biting me in
--     the ankle, proof of my wellness visit was provided 6 months after the
--     effective date, and I was serving as a police officer at the time of
--     hospitalization?
-- Judgement call (see NOTES.md): the bite did not arise directly or
-- indirectly out of police service (Section 3.1(4)) -- the claimant merely
-- happened to be a serving police officer AT THE TIME, which is a status, not
-- a cause, so that exclusion is not triggered. Confirmation at 6 months is
-- within the Section 1.3 window.
q9 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                                                       IS 30
    `months after the effective date the hospitalization occurred`                 IS 3
    `due to sickness`                                                              IS FALSE
    `due to accidental injury`                                                     IS TRUE
    `hospital located in the United States`                                        IS TRUE
    `caused by skydiving`                                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the military`                                            IS FALSE
    `caused by service as a fire fighter`                                          IS FALSE
    `caused by service in the police`                                              IS FALSE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding`                           IS FALSE
    `months after the effective date the wellness visit confirmation was supplied` IS JUST 6
    `claim made to the company with the basis for the claim stated`                IS TRUE
#EVAL `covered` q9
